  "flavor_text": {
    "one_line": "The Ithranei thrive where markets meet the surf, blending maritime daring with hardheaded civic bonds.",
    "one_paragraph": "The Ithranei inhabit harbors, estuaries, and island towns built for trade as much as defense. Their republics are noisy with auction cries, dock songs, civic rituals, and arguments over taxes, tides, and foreign privileges. They celebrate prosperity openly, yet their greatest moral test remains simple: whether one keeps faith with shipmates, harbor lights, and the city that takes in sailors from every horizon."
